### Week 5 tests (REST Client). Prerequisites: migrations 004 and 005 loaded; Week 4 test data exists
### (approved provider with Service ON + a published offer; verified student). Copy the offer id from "Provider: my offers".
@host = http://localhost:4000
@offerId = PASTE_OFFER_ID_HERE

### Provider login
# @name provider
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "provider@metrouni.edu.bd", "password": "StrongPass123" }

### Provider: my offers (copy an id)
GET {{host}}/api/offers/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{provider.response.body.token}}

### Student login
# @name student
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student@metrouni.edu.bd", "password": "StrongPass123" }

### 1. Preview (no seat taken)
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{student.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "offer_id": "{{offerId}}",
  "route": { "type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[90.3742,23.7461],[90.3900,23.7800],[90.3990,23.8759]] } }

### 2. Book (201). Sending it again with the SAME key returns the same booking (200), not a second one.
# @name booking
POST {{host}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{student.response.body.token}}
Idempotency-Key: my-first-booking-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "offer_id": "{{offerId}}",
  "route": { "type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[90.3742,23.7461],[90.3900,23.7800],[90.3990,23.8759]] } }

### 3. My bookings
GET {{host}}/api/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{student.response.body.token}}

### 4. Provider sees it too
GET {{host}}/api/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{provider.response.body.token}}

### 5. Cancel (student). Seat becomes available again.
PATCH {{host}}/api/bookings/{{booking.response.body.booking.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{student.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Class timing changed" }
